{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01P5FDCqdNLy45nNtK5V7Se6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a personal productivity + R&D mission-control system built for J.C. Liechty. Grounded in the project docs:\n\n- **Purpose:** It's a single-folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), stdlib-only personal productivity system that treats plain markdown files (DASHBOARD.md, PROJECTS.md, INBOX.md, domain files) as the source of truth â€” no database, no syncing.\n\n- **What it does (core):** Runs a persistent local web server (`anchor_gui.py`, the declared deliverable) bound to `http://localhost:8777` under the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It serves an interactive browser dashboard that reads/writes the markdown directly â€” add/check-off/edit/cancel/save tasks, capture inbox ideas â€” with a CLI mirror (`anchor.py`) and a 5 AM self-test (`anchor_healthcheck.py`).\n\n- **What it ships (the R&D surface):** Beyond task-tracking, it has grown a \"trio-driven R&D control surface\" â€” per-project cockpit windows that launch the researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman skill trio as durable, isolated server-side sessions. The current iteration (**v4 \"Project Cockpit\"**, built + merged to master 2026-06-13) renders each lane (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) as a status-lit tile that expands an inline panel: a cached summary on top, a real resizable xterm.js terminal below.\n\n- **Terminal substrate:** Real Windows **ConPTY** terminals (via the one declared native exception, `pywinpty`, lazy-imported only in `pty_manager.py`), with per-session git-worktree isolation, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini, Gemini research-only), and a skill that auto-loads/greets exactly **once** per new session (the v4 fix for the old repeating-prompt bug).\n\n- **Supporting machinery:** sessions/effort-history tracking, validated+cached session and project summaries (generate-twice + grounding filter), grass-catcher idea board with promote-to-lane, type-aware deliverable launch (skill/tool verify Â· service preview on a port â‰  8777 Â· program run Â· doc render), and Ghost World Labs branding (\"Powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢\").\n\nIn short: a markdown-backed GTD dashboard that has evolved into a mission-control cockpit for running and remembering AI-trio R&D work on each tracked project."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42ea01dd-db24-4aa9-96f0-1d6a7508ebae","uuid":"0dac5ab7-287f-4c8a-89c3-f8ec935f0987","request_id":"req_011Cc1fFY92gG3oWfQwVzCcQ"}
